title: 'relay-chain-rpc: go back to preferred connection'
doc:
- audience: Node Operator
  description: |-
    `--relay-chain-rpc-urls` is now a priority list. While on a fallback endpoint, the node checks
    the endpoints listed before it every 5 minutes and switches back to the first one that is
    reachable and has caught up with the best block, instead of staying on the fallback until that
    connection fails. Reconnecting no longer waits for requests on the old connection, and an
    endpoint whose subscriptions fail is skipped instead of stopping the node.
crates:
- name: cumulus-relay-chain-rpc-interface
  bump: patch
- name: cumulus-client-cli
  bump: patch
